Track the maximum and minimum products ending at each position, since a negative value can exchange their roles. Both updates use the previous values.

```javascript
function solve(nums) {
  let maxEnding = nums[0];
  let minEnding = nums[0];
  let best = nums[0];

  for (let i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
    const x = nums[i];
    const fromMax = x * maxEnding;
    const fromMin = x * minEnding;

    maxEnding = Math.max(x, fromMax, fromMin);
    minEnding = Math.min(x, fromMax, fromMin);
    best = Math.max(best, maxEnding);
  }

  return best;
}
```

Call solve(nums) with a nonempty numeric array. Time: O(n). Extra space: O(1).

