Store prefix products in the output, then multiply by suffix products. This handles zeros without division.

```javascript
function solve(nums) {
  const result = new Array(nums.length);
  let prefix = 1;

  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
    result[i] = prefix;
    prefix *= nums[i];
  }

  let suffix = 1;
  for (let i = nums.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    result[i] *= suffix;
    suffix *= nums[i];
  }

  return result;
}
```

Call solve(nums) directly. Time: O(n). Extra space: O(1) beyond the O(n) returned array.

